{"name":"Trade Secret","hex":"#6a7978","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"trade secret","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of intellectual property comprising confidential business information that provides a company with a competitive edge."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trade_secret"}],"entries":[{"title":"Trade secret","blocks":[{"text":"A trade secret is a type of intellectual property that protects a formula, process, or other business information that is valuable because it is not generally known or readily ascertainable and that the owner keeps secret in order to maintain a competitive advantage. Well-known examples of trade secrets include the formula for Coca-Cola, the recipe for Kentucky Fried Chicken, and the formula for Zildjian bronze cymbals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Intellectual_property_Noun_project.svg/330px-Intellectual_property_Noun_project.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trade_secret"},{"title":"Trade Secret (Australian company)","blocks":[{"text":"Trade Secret was a chain of clothing, accessories and home furnishing stores operated by TJX and had 35 stores across Australia by April 2017. The stores were located in Sydney, Melbourne, Brisbane, Canberra, Newcastle, Wollongong, Cairns, Townsville, Toowoomba, Albury, the Sunshine Coast and the Gold Coast. On 3 February 2017, they announced on their website that they would soon be rebranding all existing locations as T.K. Maxx and opening new locations across the east coast. As of 20 April 2017 the stores were operating as T.K. Maxx."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/dd/Trade_Secret_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trade_Secret_(Australian_company)"},{"title":"Trade","blocks":[{"text":"Trade is the act 